#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

usage() {
    cat <<'HELP'
Usage: startup-prompt [--json] [--weekly] [--view NAME] ...
       startup-prompt --help

Print what a session opens with: four prompts, then views of the saved
Org files under the working directory, in the ClankOS container.
"clankos-run help startup-prompt" prints the protocol.

  next                 every NEXT item: projects', responsibilities'
                       and the root's apart
  waiting              every WAITING item
  someday              every SOMEDAY item: not committed to
  scheduled            items scheduled in the next 14 days, or late
  deadlines            every open deadline, however far off
  reviews              reviews late or due in the next 7 days, projects'
                       and responsibilities' apart
  reviews-to-schedule  active projects, responsibilities and the
                       root that no review covers
  stuck                projects with STATUS WIP and no NEXT or WAITING
                       item
  projects             each active project: its status, next review,
                       next action and outcome
  intray               every open item under Unsorted in an intray.org:
                       captured and not yet placed
  finished             items closed in the last 7 days
  all                  every TODO item

With no --view, every view but someday, projects, finished and all is
printed. --view NAME, repeated, prints the prompts and those views
only. --weekly stands for the views of a weekly review: intray, next,
waiting, scheduled, deadlines, reviews, stuck, reviews-to-schedule,
someday, finished. --json prints the views as one line of JSON in
place of the text.

Reads; writes nothing. The files are those the configuration allows:
not the excluded directories, archives and attics by default. A
product's Org files are read. The
working directory's pos-config.el, if it has one, is loaded and can
change the horizons.

Exit: 0 printed, 2 usage, 255 Emacs error, its message on stderr; 125,
126 and 127 are clankos-run's.
HELP
}

case "${1:-}" in
    help|-h|--help) usage; exit 0 ;;
esac
exec "$(cd -- "$(dirname -- "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/clankos-run" startup-prompt "$@"
